        "original_id": "278f099b-9ed6-5249-85a3-263766401f49",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Products: Korean Jindo, Taigan, Nureongi\n- Organizations: United Kennel Club, Fédération Cynologique Internationale, national kennel clubs\n- Places: Korea, Kyrgyzstan, Central Asia\n- Concepts: dog breed recognition, sighthounds, spitz dogs, Salburun, falconry, archery, mounted archery, hunting\n\nFacts:\n- The Korean Jindo breed was recognized by the United Kennel Club on January 1, 1998.\n- The Korean Jindo breed was recognized by the Fédération Cynologique Internationale in 2005.\n- The Taigan is a sighthound breed from Kyrgyzstan.\n- The Taigan is also known as Kyrgyzdyn Taighany and as Kyrgyzskaya Borzaya Taigan in Russian.\n- The Taigan is not recognized by the Fédération Cynologique Internationale, but it is recognized by a number of kennel clubs at the national level.\n- Nureongi and the Korean Jindo are native Korean dogs.\n- Korean Yellow spitzes are medium-sized spitz dogs with greater musculature and distinctive coat patterns.\n- Salburun is a traditional kind of hunt in Kyrgyzstan and Central Asia.\n- Salburun involves falconry, archery, sometimes mounted archery, and hunting with Taigan.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "f6956279-87e5-50e7-8383-ee8fa7b71232",
        "text": "Page: Korean Jindo. Sentence: The Jindo breed became recognized by the United Kennel Club on January 1, 1998 and by the Fédération Cynologique Internationale in 2005.\nPage: Taigan. Sentence: The Taigan (Kyrgyz: Тайган ) also known as Kyrgyzdyn Taighany (Kyrgyzskaya Borzaya Taigan in Russian) is a sighthound breed from Kyrgyzstan, which is not yet recognized by the FCI, but is recognized by a number of kennel clubs on national level.\nPage: Nureongi. Sentence: Like native Korean dogs such as the Korean Jindo, Korean Yellow spitzes are medium-sized spitz, but with greater musculature and distinctive coat patterns.\nPage: Salburun. Sentence: Salburun (Kyrgyz : Салбуурун) is a traditional kind of hunt in Kyrghyzstan and Central Asia, involving falconry, archery and sometimes mounted archery, as well as hunting with Taigan.",
